// the reason before the keyword: "since R, exhaustive cases", then a closer in the user's words
let n in Z. wts n^2 is congruent to 0 or 1 mod 4
since n is either even or odd, exhaustive cases
case n is even. then n = 2m, so n^2 = 4m^2 ≡ 0 mod 4.
case n is odd. then n = 2m + 1, so n^2 = 4(m^2 + m) + 1 ≡ 1 mod 4.
in all exhaustive cases, n^2 ≡ 0 or n^2 ≡ 1 mod 4.
qed
